    "vanilla_policy": "All natural Overworld spawn lists are cleared in POST_PROCESSING, then explicit Haute Capitale fauna is re-added in the SAME phase, after the clear.",
    "marine_policy": "Strict swimming fauna is handled by aquatic_runtime_rules.json. Thornshell remains amphibious and uses thornshell_behavior_rules.json for bottom-walking/shore-exit behavior.",
    "hmobs_policy": "HMobs is bundled in 1.2.12; its original natural weights/groups are reproduced in the authoritative datapack because the Haute Capitale controller clears/rebuilds Overworld spawn lists.",
    "orc_policy": "General Overworld orcs remain event-only through orc_patrol_rules.json. Natural orc populations are restricted to #capitale_creatures:orc_dungeon and bounded by orc_dungeon_rules.json.",
    "cultural_biomes": "BETA 0.16 narrows terrestrial habitat tags to the validated cultural geography: Empire, Elves, Nordics and Dwarves. Desert/badlands remain the provisional Orc dry territory. Cities and corruption are excluded from ordinary wildlife.",
    "everywhere_surface": "Rules historically described as 'everywhere' now target #capitale_creatures:cultural_surface_land rather than #capitale_creatures:all_overworld. all_overworld stays broad because the controller still needs it for global vanilla/mod spawn clearing.",
    "user_cultural_fauna": "BETA 0.17 applies the user's preserved cultural-fauna assignments to entities already active. Planned new entities (white unicorn, Aeternae, Capella, Cyclops, Minotaur, Crocotta, Argan Hound, Droughtroot Forest Hag, Revenants, Arachne Drone and Snull) remain inactive until manual validation."
